Rust compilation with `--recursive-modules` now supports empty arrays without
an element initializer, including dynamic zero extents and recursive datatype
elements. Dimensions are evaluated once in order. For auto-initializable elements, a runtime check also prevents
nonempty uninitialized allocations when verification is skipped; verified
nonempty arrays still require an explicit initializer under `--enforce-determinism`.
Compilation without a recursive group is unchanged.
